79,"k":"block","t":"Yandex Cloud Translate v2","f":[]},{"s":41689,"e":41781,"k":"block","t":"Needs a KTPH000service account API keyKTPH001 from Yandex Cloud, not the retired v1.5 key","f":["<strong>","</strong>"]},{"s":41872,"e":41919,"k":"block","t":"Yandex keys stored by an earlier korTTY version","f":[]},{"s":41927,"e":42614,"k":"block","t":"Yandex stopped issuing keys for the old Translate API v1.5 and switched off the free keys it\nhad already issued, so no obtainable v1.5 key authenticates any more. korTTY now talks to the\nYandex Cloud Translate v2 endpoint instead, and a v1.5 key stored in an earlier korTTY version\nwill not work: create a service account in the Yandex Cloud console, give it the\nKTPH000 role, issue an API key for it, and paste that key into\nKTPH002Settings → TranslationKTPH003. If you also filled in the KTPH004API URLKTPH005 field with the old\nKTPH001 address, clear it — korTTY ignores that address and logs a\nwarning until you do.","f":["<code>ai.translate.user</code>","<code>translate.yandex.net/api/v1.5/...</code>","<strong>","</strong>","<strong>","</strong>"]},{"s":42660,"e":42772,"k":"block","t":"Generating a TranslationKTPH000","f":["<a class=\"headerlink\" href=\"#generating-a-translation\" title=\"Permanent link\">&para;</a>"]},{"s":42781,"e":42825,"k":"block","t":"To generate translations for a new language:","f":[]},{"s":42839,"e":42883,"k":"block","t":"Open KTPH000Settings → TranslationKTPH001","f":["<strong>","</strong>"]},{"s":42893,"e":42952,"k":"block","t":"Choose a KTPH000Translation APIKTPH001 from the dropdown","f":["<strong>","</strong>"]},{"s":42962,"e":43048,"k":"block","t":"Enter your API key if required (the key is stored encrypted with your master password)","f":[]},{"s":43058,"e":43171,"k":"block","t":"Optionally set a KTPH000custom API URLKTPH001 (for example, to point to a self-hosted LibreTranslate instance)","f":["<strong>","</strong>"]},{"s":43181,"e":43249,"k":"block","t":"Click KTPH000Test API ConnectionKTPH001 to verify the setup works","f":["<strong>","</strong>"]},{"s":43259,"e":43329,"k":"block","t":"Select the KTPH000target languageKTPH001 from the language dropdown","f":["<strong>","</strong>"]},{"s":43339,"e":43384,"k":"block","t":"Click KTPH000Generate Language FileKTPH001","f":["<strong>","</strong>"]},{"s":43399,"e":43663,"k":"block","t":"The generated language file is saved to KTPH000, where KTPH001 is the two-letter language code. After generation, restart the application to make the new language available in KTPH002Settings → LanguageKTPH003.","f":["<code>~/.kortty/i18n/messages_XX.properties</code>","<code>XX</code>","<strong>","</strong>"]},{"s":43696,"e":43796,"k":"block","t":"After App UpgradesKTPH000","f":["<a class=\"headerlink\" href=\"#after-app-upgrades\" title=\"Permanent link\">&para;</a>"]},{"s":43805,"e":44072,"k":"block","t":"When KorTTY is upgraded to a new version, previously generated language files are automatically detected as outdated if they were created with an older app version. In KTPH000Settings → TranslationKTPH001, a notice appears indicating which languages need updating.","f":["<strong>","</strong>"]},{"s":44080,"e":44136,"k":"block","t":"To refresh all outdated language files after an upgrade:","f":[]},{"s":44150,"e":44194,"k":"block","t":"Open KTPH000Settings → TranslationKTPH001","f":["<strong>","</strong>"]},{"s":44204,"e":44246,"k":"block","t":"Click KTPH000Regenerate outdatedKTPH001","f":["<strong>","</strong>"]},{"s":44256,"e":44349,"k":"block","t":"All generated languages are re-translated to include new or changed keys from the new version","f":[]},{"s":44364,"e":44630,"k":"block","t":"Regenerating is not urgent: until you do it, any string added after your file was generated falls back to the packaged translation for that language, or to English when the language ships no packaged file. You see a translated or English label, never a raw key name.","f":[]},{"s":44668,"e":44778,"k":"block","t":"Storage and PersistenceKTPH000","f":["<a class=\"headerlink\" href=\"#storage-and-persistence\" title=\"Permanent link\">&para;</a>"]},{"s":44793,"e":44860,"k":"block","t":"Generated language files are stored in KTPH000","f":["<code>~/.kortty/i18n/</code>"]},{"s":44870,"e":44939,"k":"block","t":"Each file is a standard Java properties file (messages_XX.properties)","f":[]},{"s":44949,"e":45002,"k":"block","t":"Files persist across application restarts and updates","f":[]},{"s":45012,"e":45110,"k":"block","t":"Language files are included in encrypted backups created via KTPH000Edit → Create BackupKTPH001","f":["<strong>","</strong>"]},{"s":45144,"e":45232,"k":"block","t":"How It WorksKTPH000","f":["<a class=\"headerlink\" href=\"#how-it-works\" title=\"Permanent link\">&para;</a>"]},{"s":45241,"e":45325,"k":"block","t":"KorTTY's internationalization system is built around a resource bundle architecture:","f":[]},{"s":45339,"e":45468,"k":"block","t":"KTPH001Base languageKTPH002: English strings are defined in KTPH000 bundled with the application","f":["<code>i18n/messages.properties</code>","<strong>","</strong>"]},{"s":45478,"e":45580,"k":"block","t":"KTPH000Built-in languagesKTPH001: Pre-translated properties files are packaged with the application","f":["<strong>","</strong>"]},{"s":45590,"e":45708,"k":"block","t":"KTPH001Dynamic languagesKTPH002: Generated properties files are loaded from KTPH000 on startup","f":["<code>~/.kortty/i18n/</code>","<strong>","</strong>"]},{"s":45718,"e":45902,"k":"block","t":"KTPH003Placeholder preservationKTPH004: Translation APIs preserve parameterized placeholders like KTPH000, KTPH001, and KTPH002 during translation","f":["<code>{0}</code>","<code>{1}</code>","<code>${variable}</code>","<strong>","</strong>"]},{"s":45912,"e":46130,"k":"block","t":"KTPH001Lookup fallbackKTPH002: A file in KTPH000 is consulted first, then the packaged file for the same language, then the English base bundle — so a key the generated file lacks still resolves","f":["<code>~/.kortty/i18n/</code>","<strong>","</strong>"]},{"s":46145,"e":46317,"k":"block","t":"The KTPH000 class detects available locales from both built-in translations and dynamically generated files, allowing you to seamlessly mix both types.","f":["<code>LanguageManager</code>"]},{"s":46357,"e":46471,"k":"block","t":"Platform Locale DetectionKTPH000","f":["<a class=\"headerlink\" href=\"#platform-locale-detection\" title=\"Permanent link\">&para;</a>"]},{"s":46480,"e":46622,"k":"block","t":"KorTTY uses your operating system's locale settings as the default when auto-detect is enabled. The language detection works across platforms:","f":[]},{"s":46636,"e":46705,"k":"block","t":"KTPH000macOSKTPH001: Reads system language from System Preferences","f":["<strong>","</strong>"]},{"s":46715,"e":46771,"k":"block","t":"KTPH000WindowsKTPH001: Uses Windows language settings","f":["<strong>","</strong>"]},{"s":46781,"e":46883,"k":"block","t":"KTPH001LinuxKTPH002: Respects the KTPH000 environment variable and system locale settings","f":["<code>LANG</code>","<strong>","</strong>"]},{"s":46898,"e":47008,"k":"block","t":"If your system's primary language is not in the built-in or generated list, English is automatically selected.","f":[]},{"s":47051,"e":47171,"k":"block","t":"Tips for Translation QualityKTPH000","f":["<a class=\"headerlink\" href=\"#tips-for-translation-quality\" title=\"Permanent link\">&para;</a>"]},{"s":47234,"e":47264,"k":"block","t":"Optimizing Translation Results","f":[]},{"s":47278,"e":47420,"k":"block","t":"KTPH000Shorter chunksKTPH001: Translation APIs work best with moderately sized strings; KorTTY batches translations in groups of 25 strings","f":["<strong>","</strong>"]},{"s":47430,"e":47584,"k":"block","t":"KTPH002Placeholder safetyKTPH003: Placeholders (KTPH000, KTPH001) are automatically protected during translation and never altered","f":["<code>{0}</code>","<code>${var}</code>","<strong>","</strong>"]},{"s":47594,"e":47776,"k":"block","t":"KTPH000Test after generationKTPH001: After generating a new language, review the interface for any awkward phrasing and consider adjusting API providers if quality is insufficient","f":["<strong>","</strong>"]},{"s":47853,"e":47880,"k":"block","t":"LibreTranslate Self-Hosting","f":[]},{"s":47888,"e":48084,"k":"block","t":"If you run a self-hosted LibreTranslate instance, you can point KorTTY to it by entering the custom API URL in the translation settings. This avoids API key dependencies and keeps your data local.","f":[]},{"s":48121,"e":48215,"k":"block","t":"TroubleshootingKTPH000","f":["<a class=\"headerlink\" href=\"#troubleshooting\" title=\"Permanent link\">&para;</a>"]},{"s":48282,"e":48303,"k":"block","t":"API Connection Issues","f":[]},{"s":48311,"e":48564,"k":"block","t":"If KTPH000Test API ConnectionKTPH001 fails, verify:\n- Your API key is correct and valid\n- The API provider's service is not experiencing outages\n- Your network can reach the API endpoint\n- For custom URLs, ensure the endpoint is reachable and running","f":["<strong>","</strong>"]},{"s":48637,"e":48668,"k":"block","t":"Missing Languages After Upgrade","f":[]},{"s":48676,"e":49015,"k":"block","t":"If a generated language file disappears after upgrading KorTTY:\n- Check that the file still exists at KTPH000\n- Verify that the app version recorded in the file matches the current app version\n- Regenerate the language using KTPH001Settings → Translation → Regenerate outdatedKTPH002 if needed","f":["<code>~/.kortty/i18n/messages_XX.properties</code>","<strong>","</strong>"]},{"s":49900,"e":49915,"k":"text","t":"\n  Back to top\n","f":[]},{"s":50158,"e":50199,"k":"text","t":"MIT-licensed · Developed by Daniel Mengel","f":[]},{"s":50245,"e":50257,"k":"text","t":"\n    korTTY ","f":[]},{"s":50265,"e":50272,"k":"text","t":"v2.14.0","f":[]}]}